  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LightShadow.UI.QuestionData
  question: Why did books become much cheaper in Europe after the 1440s?
  options:
  - Paper was invented in Europe then
  - Printing presses copied texts far faster than scribes could
  - Books became smaller
  - Authors started writing faster
  correctIndex: 1
  category: 2
  difficulty: 2
  explanation: Gutenberg's printing press (around 1440) could produce copies far
    more quickly than hand-copying, so prices fell.
